From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:06:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] security/tpm: 256 KiB for the TPM 1.2 log a payload appends
 to

The TPM 1.2 log in cbmem, which the ACPI TCPA table publishes as its log
area, is where a UEFI payload (SecurityPkg TcgDxe) logs its events after
coreboot's; it got the 64 KiB that acpi.c gives a TCPA log. On a
ThinkCentre M920x with the same payload and a TPM 2.0, its log area of
64 KiB (EDK2's default PcdTcgLogAreaMinLen) was full before
ExitBootServices: the Secure Boot variables (dbx alone 21 KiB), the
boot variables, shim's and GRUB's events (GRUB measures each command it
runs). The events after that extend the PCRs and are not logged, and
the log no longer replays to them (PCR 5 there).

Give the TPM 1.2 log 256 KiB, as ouroBIOS gives Tcg2Dxe on the TPM 2.0
side.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c b/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c
index e807b2547a..14886ea820 100644
--- a/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c
+++ b/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c
@@ -32,10 +32,12 @@ void *tpm1_log_cbmem_init(void)
 		/*
 		 * This table is also the log area of the ACPI TCPA table, where
 		 * a UEFI payload logs its own events after coreboot's: leave
-		 * room for them, as much as acpi.c gives a log of its own.
+		 * room for them. The Secure Boot variables, the boot loader's
+		 * events (GRUB measures its commands) and the OS loader's can
+		 * take more than the 64 KiB acpi.c gives a log of its own.
 		 */
 		tpm_log_len = MAX(sizeof(*tclt) + MAX_TPM_LOG_ENTRIES * sizeof(tclt->entries[0]),
-				  64 * KiB);
+				  256 * KiB);
 		tclt = cbmem_add(CBMEM_ID_TCPA_TCG_LOG, tpm_log_len);
 		if (!tclt)
 			return NULL;
